@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Tasks are known only by their title, and a title changes when a task is renamed. The app needs a stable
+reference to a task that keeps working after a rename.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets an `id`: a string no other task of the list has, set by `add`.
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning the task as a `Result`, like the other methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: each task has a stable unique id, which can be used to look up and act on the task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts` (`Task` gains `id`), `src/domain/list.ts` (id generation, `get`, id-or-title lookup).
+- `test/list.test.ts`: the test comparing an added task whole needs the `id`.
+- No new dependency; the public API in `src/index.ts` only grows.
